 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Stein factorization",
 "statement": "Let $p:Y\\to S=\\operatorname{Spec}A$ be a proper\n[def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions] morphism with $A$ a commutative ring. Put\n$B=H^0(Y,\\mathcal O_Y)$, a ring under the $A$-algebra structure induced by\n$p$, and let $q:Y\\to\\operatorname{Spec}B$ be the canonical morphism and\n$s:\\operatorname{Spec}B\\to\\operatorname{Spec}A$ the morphism of the algebra\nstructure, so that $p=s\\circ q$. The factorization\n\n$$\n Y\\xrightarrow{\\ q\\ }\\operatorname{Spec}B\\xrightarrow{\\ s\\ }\\operatorname{Spec}A\n$$\n\nis the *Stein factorization* of $p$ (*source: Stacks Project, More on\nMorphisms, Section 37.53, Tag\n[03GX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GX)*).",
 "source": {
